			]
			tasks: [
				{ id: "1279EE6E3E035D74", item: "gtceu:hot_trinium_ingot", type: "item" }
				{ id: "5DA8897D462037B9", item: "gtceu:trinium_ingot", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Trinium"
			x: 6.0d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3C825200F07FFF67"]
			description: ["Enriched naquadah becomes long rods for GT--'s &6Naquadah Reactor III&r, the fuel-burning half of LuV power. A spent rod isn't rubbish: macerate it and send the dust back to the plant's spent-fuel recipe, which squeezes some enriched naquadah back out. Not all of it, sadly."]
			icon: "gtnn:luv_naquadah_reactor"
			id: "3D5EC5039EBDE967"
			rewards: [{ id: "56651F15A5E42E03", type: "xp", xp: 80 }]
			tasks: [
				{ id: "3B8544C7C67CEA61", item: "gtnn:luv_naquadah_reactor", type: "item" }
				{ id: "3AF3F461B1F975EC", item: "gtceu:long_enriched_naquadah_rod", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Reactor III"
			x: 4.0d
			y: -4.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3C825200F07FFF67"]
			description: ["The &6LuV Parallel Hatch&r fits the same slot as the IV one in every plant of ours, the naquadah plant included. Each copy still pays its own power, so it's your energy hatches that decide how many really run, and multi-amp hatches lift that cap."]
			icon: "gtceu:luv_parallel_hatch"
			id: "548A6D01CD361BD3"
			optional: true
			rewards: [{ id: "5120C35F3DE3D903", type: "xp", xp: 60 }]
			size: 0.75d
			tasks: [{ id: "305D8E0FD477DA5A", item: "gtceu:luv_parallel_hatch", type: "item" }]
			title: "Sixteen at Once"
			x: 6.0d
			y: -3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7A00F7E4F256E45A"]
			description: [
				"Every hot ingot in the vacuum freezer throws half its liquid helium away. The &6Helium Refrigerator&r keeps a helium charge in its own hatch and only tops it up, with liquid nitrogen doing the precooling."
				"The nitrogen leaves as gas: send it back to the Moon's cryogenic plant."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:helium_refrigerator"
			id: "1368397CE117ECD1"
			rewards: [
				{ id: "51143C2CFF164BCA", type: "xp", xp: 80 }
				{ count: 4, id: "32DEC6633BEFD989", item: "gtceu:liquid_nitrogen_bucket", type: "item" }
			]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [{ id: "1C61E246579AA5DD", item: "gtceu:helium_refrigerator", type: "item" }]
			title: "Closed Loop"
			x: 4.0d
			y: 1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7A00F7E4F256E45A"]
			description: [
				"GregTech's sterile chain normally waits for a ZPM cleanroom. The &6Biofoundry&r is a sealed hall with an airlock and a UV ceiling, and it runs the whole chain at LuV, starting from your creature simulators' meat and bone."
				"Collagen, gelatin and agar need nothing alive. Everything after them needs bacteria, and Earth hasn't got any you can use."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:biofoundry"
			id: "3B64E8E2A5FD37A0"
			rewards: [
				{ id: "3ABC85FC87C82788", type: "xp", xp: 80 }
				{ count: 16, id: "33AF14918A101674", item: "minecraft:bone", type: "item" }
			]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "5DA2D5A6129F14AA", item: "gtceu:biofoundry", type: "item" }
				{ id: "5110D841416DB276", item: "gtceu:gelatin_dust", type: "item" }
				{ id: "588877DE57E0E365", item: "gtceu:agar_dust", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Biofoundry"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5933ADF51C8949BD"]
			description: [
				"GCYR's &6Space Station Packager&r folds a whole station into one package small enough for a rocket. Pack it at home, fly it to Earth orbit and open it there; the GregTech machines go in once you've arrived."
				"Everything up there draws from the wireless network, which is why the network came first."
			]
			icon: "gcyr:space_station_packager"
			id: "531171ADA3A1A60B"
			rewards: [{ id: "705E817367653C3C", type: "xp", xp: 80 }]
			tasks: [
				{ id: "7378F46BB42CBD46", item: "gcyr:space_station_packager", type: "item" }
				{ id: "10E8129E34FC8F81", item: "gcyr:space_station_package", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Packed and Launched"
			x: 12.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["531171ADA3A1A60B"]
			description: ["Earth orbit: no air, no night, and the coldest shade you'll ever stand in. Chunk-load the station, or its machines stop the moment you fly home."]
			icon: "grindless:station_truss_casing"
			id: "75745AD963ECB5C8"
			rewards: [{ id: "349D03BE358D5C31", type: "xp", xp: 100 }]
			shape: "rsquare"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [{ dimension: "gcyr:overworld_orbit", id: "5CA94CD95613248B", type: "dimension" }]
			title: "First Station"
			x: 14.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["75745AD963ECB5C8"]
			description: [
				"Up here the Sun never sets, and the &6Orbital Solar Station&r makes the most of it: two wings of panels on a truss, and every panel that sees open sky pays. Send the power home through a LuV wireless dynamo hatch."
				"It burns nothing, so nothing doubles it."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:orbital_solar_station"
			id: "3F2030C8DDEDB9FF"
			rewards: [
				{ id: "39623E31E54F56E3", type: "xp", xp: 100 }
				{ count: 2, id: "18F7447DC3B656EE", item: "gcyr:photovoltaic_cell", type: "item" }
			]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "7DCDEB7079BC07A6", item: "gtceu:orbital_solar_station", type: "item" }
				{ id: "32FE0E13005F7F83", item: "grindless:orbital_solar_panel", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Endless Day"
			x: 16.0d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["75745AD963ECB5C8"]
			description: [
				"On the ground ZBLAN glass crystallizes while it's drawn; up here it stays clear. The &6Microgravity Smelter&r draws it into optical pipe with no silver at all, foams metal into Whipple shield casing and melts naquadah alloy floating in a field, no crucible."
				"Mix the ZBLAN at home in the Large Mixing Vessel: a normal mixer can't hold that much fluorine."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:microgravity_smelter"
			id: "121BEE9B7E15DE8C"
			rewards: [{ id: "3FF36420AFEFE3A2", type: "xp", xp: 100 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "36718AA56A92385A", item: "gtceu:microgravity_smelter", type: "item" }
				{ id: "135209E83A9A320B", item: "gtceu:zblan_dust", type: "item" }
				{ id: "3A96E3076111AE91", item: "gtceu:normal_optical_pipe", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Fibre from Nothing"
			x: 16.0d
			y: -3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["121BEE9B7E15DE8C"]
			description: [
				"Behind a disc flying through orbit, the vacuum is emptier than any chamber you could build. The &6Wake Shield Facility&r grows HPIC and UHPIC wafers there with half the source and half the time."
				"Its disc is Whipple shield casing, so the smelter goes first. Give it germanium and it grows solar wafers too."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:wake_shield_facility"
			id: "58EFB73E6DD24BDB"
			rewards: [
				{ id: "5917C4380DC0402D", type: "xp", xp: 100 }
				{ count: 4, id: "3AEEC37901F33633", item: "gtceu:indium_gallium_phosphide_dust", type: "item" }
			]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "54780AE195859BCD", item: "gtceu:wake_shield_facility", type: "item" }
				{ id: "381B7ED8F85D18FD", item: "gtceu:uhpic_wafer", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "In the Wake"
			x: 18.0d
			y: -3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["75745AD963ECB5C8"]
			description: [
				"With nothing stirring the melt, a crystal grows without flaws. The &6Zero-G Crystal Grower&r makes raw crystal chips every time instead of now and then, and much faster, with the same dopant GregTech asks for."
				"Its sapphire test masses are for later; EMI says what for."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:zero_g_crystal_grower"
			id: "18A794C8BAA71D81"
			rewards: [
				{ id: "79A3343DDCAA87FC", type: "xp", xp: 100 }
				{ count: 16, id: "70CB42BE6A87A4A8", item: "gtceu:sapphire_dust", type: "item" }
			]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "36BE5E6C87916B16", item: "gtceu:zero_g_crystal_grower", type: "item" }
				{ id: "5132B223B09F2DD4", item: "grindless:sapphire_test_mass", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Perfect Crystal"
			x: 16.0d
			y: 1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["38F8454E1AEB4E72"]
			description: [
				"GregTech's &6Fusion Reactor Mk1&r, built round your own HTS coils. Every energy hatch adds to the buffer that pays for a start, and europium needs a big start, so fit plenty of LuV hatches."
				"At LuV it's a materials machine first: the old transmutations that faked osmium and uranium are gone, and calcium plasma from magnesium and oxygen is its power recipe."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:luv_fusion_reactor"
			id: "543F014BB97A45F4"
			rewards: [{ id: "533D64890831EDCA", type: "xp", xp: 150 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "325918310E498A2C", item: "gtceu:luv_fusion_reactor", type: "item" }
				{ count: 4L, id: "5A26D33DF72BC1E3", item: "gtceu:superconducting_coil", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Fusion"
			x: 10.0d
			y: 3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["543F014BB97A45F4"]
			description: ["Mars's neodymium and plain hydrogen go in, &6Europium&r comes out, and nothing else in the pack makes it. It leaves the ring as a very hot liquid, not a plasma, so pipe it accordingly. The ZPM motor wants a lot of it as fine wire."]
			icon: "gtceu:europium_ingot"
			id: "1531C1737C6BE31B"
			rewards: [{ id: "78D7DB85185F24E8", type: "xp", xp: 100 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "3FA5997B75AD7194", item: "gtceu:europium_ingot", type: "item" }]
			title: "Europium"
			x: 12.0d
			y: 3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["1531C1737C6BE31B"]
			description: [
				"The &6Research Station&r and the HPCA turn computation into data orbs, and the first one worth writing is the ZPM energy hatch's. Their wiring needs the large mixer on two LuV hatches, and the europium went into the station's ZPM motors."
				"Computer casings, a data bank and plenty of optical pipe come first."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:research_station"
			id: "32CEA916CCFD8B21"
			rewards: [
				{ id: "1542FA63425C2185", type: "xp", xp: 150 }
